```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
• 2result.sql explicitly filters out LOCALIZER images and JPEG‑compressed transfer syntaxes, keeps only CT modality and excludes the “nlst” collection.  
• It checks every requested per‑series consistency property: unique ImageOrientationPatient, PixelSpacing, Rows/Columns, identical x‑ and y‑ in‑plane positions, constant slice spacing (n_unique_dz = 1), identical exposure (n_exptime = 1), and confirms that image count equals the number of unique z‑positions.  
• It verifies the orientation cross‑product |cz| between 0.99 and 1.01.  
• It then orders by the summed series size (MiB) and limits to the top 5.  

1result.sql omits several mandatory checks—LOCALIZER filtering, slice‑spacing regularity, exposure consistency—and therefore can return series that violate the specification, whereas 2result.sql satisfies the full set of stated requirements.